      "content": "First and foremost, your symptoms of lightheadedness and anxiety could indicate an adverse reaction to ammonia, heavy metals, or mold spores, so you should stop using the mist area and consult a medical professional immediately. Since air pollution from neighbors is your responsibility, you can install a HEPA and activated carbon filter on your home's HVAC system or use portable air purifiers in windows to remove particulates before they enter your building. If the installation itself is faulty or dangerous, you should document your symptoms and contact your local health department or the neighbor's homeowner's association to request an inspection. Prioritizing your immediate safety through filtration and professional medical advice is the most effective first step.",
