      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Activated carbon filters, specifically those designated \"UL\" for organic compounds, are significantly more effective than standard HEPA at adsorbing volatile organic compounds and altering agricultural odors. While true \"chemi-neutralizers\" are rare for outdoor pests, carbon beds with high surface area and specific impregnation can trap these complex molecules within your personal air purifier. You should consider higher capacities due to the high air volume generated by the heavy mist, as over-saturation will render them less effective. Given your specific concerns, purchasing a robust localized purification system and documenting the misting schedule will strengthen your case if you need to report this to the neighbor or authorities.",
